 ## Overview
-Nerfiller is a method for 3D scene completion using arbitrary masks, leveraging a grid-based prior and an iterative distillation framework [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like [Reference-guided Controllable Inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields](15289-reference-guided-controllable-inpainting-of-neural-radiance-.md) and [Masked Completion via GAN Inversion](20185-masked-completion-via-gan-inversion.md) by explicitly shuffling rendered images into 2x2 grids to feed into 2D inpainting diffusion models, thereby enforcing 3D consistency through multi-view scoring [S1]. While [Masked Completion via GAN Inversion](20185-masked-completion-via-gan-inversion.md) relies on GAN inversion for completion, Nerfiller uses diffusion priors to generate harmonious completions for large, arbitrary masked regions [S1].
+Nerfiller is a method for 3D scene completion using arbitrary masks, leveraging a grid-based prior and an iterative distillation framework [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like [Reference-guided Controllable Inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields](15289-reference-guided-controllable-inpainting-of-neural-radiance-.md) and [Masked Completion via GAN Inversion](20185-masked-completion-via-gan-inversion.md) by explicitly shuffling rendered images into $2 \times 2$ grids to feed into 2D inpainting diffusion models, thereby enforcing 3D consistency through multi-view scoring [S1]. While [Masked Completion via GAN Inversion](20185-masked-completion-via-gan-inversion.md) relies on GAN inversion for completion, Nerfiller uses diffusion priors to generate harmonious completions for large, arbitrary masked regions [S1].
 
